<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kediri Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kediri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kediri Kingdom was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-buddhist">Hindu-Buddhist</a> state in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> that flourished in the eleventh and twelfth centuries. Its rise, followed by that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>, created a powerful rival centre in the region. This shift contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom.jpg" alt="Kediri Kingdom" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southeast_Asia_trade_route_map_XIIcentury.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
